00:00:07.697 --> 00:00:10.030
IBRAHIM ULUKAYA: It seems
machine learning is everywhere

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:11.100
nowadays.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.130
And with so many offerings
for you as a mobile developer,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:19.180
it can get really confusing
as to where you should start.

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.540
I'm Ibrahim Ulukaya, an
engineer on the Firebase team,

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.630
and I'm here today to introduce
you to the options that

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.460
are available to you.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.160
If we could carry data
centers in our pocket

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:33.310
with unlimited battery,
it will be much easier.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.070
But using ML for
mobile apps means

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:39.970
thinking about the processing
power, battery consumption,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:43.370
and connectivity of our device.

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.980
There are a number
of factors that

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.240
will dictate the ML strategy
and tools you'll want to use,

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.970
like whether you want
to keep the data local,

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:55.720
if you require low latency,
or if you need access

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.870
to the processing
power of the cloud.

00:00:58.870 --> 00:01:02.200
Luckily, Google offers
a number of ML options

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.660
for mobile developers
that can help

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:09.460
you develop and deploy ML
models for the environment that

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:11.740
fits your use case.

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.940
To help you pick which ML
deployment option fits best,

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.900
I'll walk you through a
few key decision points.

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:22.210
The first question you
should ask yourself

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:26.050
is where you want to
perform ML inferences--

00:01:26.050 --> 00:01:28.870
in the cloud or on the device?

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:32.620
You would use a cloud if you are
already using an existing cloud

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:35.790
service for model inferences.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.590
Or you run inferences
infrequently

00:01:38.590 --> 00:01:42.880
and want to minimize impact
on the device battery life.

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:47.980
Or need to support older,
less performant devices.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.250
Or if you need high-accuracy
models that require

00:01:51.250 --> 00:01:53.980
the compute power of the cloud.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.840
On the other hand,
there are cases

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:58.300
in which it might
be useful to do ML

00:01:58.300 --> 00:02:01.210
inference on the mobile device.

00:02:01.210 --> 00:02:05.920
For example, if you want to
keep data local to the device.

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:10.300
You need low latency, such as
RAM processing multiple frames

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.190
in quick succession.

00:02:12.190 --> 00:02:16.930
You want inferences to work
even when the device is offline.

00:02:16.930 --> 00:02:20.170
Or your users may be
in an area of the world

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.900
where high-speed
wireless connectivity

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.150
is non-existent or unreliable.

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.680
So now that you understand
all the considerations,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:33.320
let me present the
options available to you.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:36.750
First is to run
inference in the cloud.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.480
And there's a wealth of
tools and APIs you can use.

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:44.170
These include Cloud Vision
for image recognition

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.380
and classification,
Cloud Natural Language

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:51.610
API for text parsing
and analysis,

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:54.880
AutoML, that allows
you to customize models

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:57.440
that are served from the cloud.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.190
All are available via REST APIs.

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.490
I won't go into them all
here, but you can learn more

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:07.120
at cloud.google.com
/products/ai/building-blocks.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.330
Next is to run
inference on the device.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.350
And you have two main options.

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:20.230
You can either use
TF Lite directly

00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:23.280
or you can use ML
Kit for Firebase.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.040
ML Kit is a mobile SDK that
brings Google's machine

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.220
learning experience
to Android and iOS

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:34.540
apps in a powerful yet
easy to use package.

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:37.330
It comes with a set
of ready to use APIs,

00:03:37.330 --> 00:03:40.810
both for on device and
cloud-based inference.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.910
They support common
mobile use cases,

00:03:42.910 --> 00:03:48.400
like image labeling, face
detection, text recognition,

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:51.140
and barcode scanning,
to name a few.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:54.430
You simply pass in the
data to the ML Kit library

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:57.070
and it will give you the
information you need.

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.700
Whether you are new to or
experienced with machine

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.790
learning, you can implement
the functionality you need, all

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:06.020
in a few lines of code.

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:09.680
And it includes both
Android and iOS libraries.

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:13.340
[? While the ?] on device
APIs process data quickly

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.110
and will work even when
there's no network connection.

00:04:17.110 --> 00:04:19.450
The cloud-based APIs
leverage the power

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:21.970
of Google Cloud
platform's machine

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:26.320
learning technology to give
a higher level of accuracy.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:30.230
If you have a use case that's
different than offered models,

00:04:30.230 --> 00:04:34.270
ML Kit also offers the ability
to deploy and experiment

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.690
with your own custom
TensorFlow Lite models

00:04:37.690 --> 00:04:41.010
to run on device inference.

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.810
It works like this.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:46.500
After converting your model
to the TF Lite format,

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.190
you can host and serve
it to your users.

00:04:50.190 --> 00:04:54.390
ML Kit for Firebase can
then be used to host

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:58.720
and dynamically serve TF
Lite models to your users.

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:01.140
And it provides
convenient APIs that

00:05:01.140 --> 00:05:06.390
help you use your custom TF
Lite models in your mobile apps.

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:09.060
With ML Kit for
Firebase, you can

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.300
reduce the initial install
size of your mobile app

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.300
and only download the
model when needed.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.730
Dynamically swap
models on the fly

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:21.480
without having to republish
you app to the app store.

00:05:21.480 --> 00:05:25.050
Target different user
segments with models

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:27.990
tailored specifically for them.

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:31.320
Run A/B experiments
with multiple models

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:33.960
to find the best-performing one.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:36.930
If you'd like, you can
also use your TF Lite

00:05:36.930 --> 00:05:41.220
model on mobile directly
with TF Lite APIs.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.650
These offer blazingly
fast inference times,

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:48.990
particularly on Android devices
that support the neural network

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:53.670
APIs and the variety of ways
to host and deploy your model.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:57.120
For mobile developers looking
to implement machine learning

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.060
into their apps, there
are several directions

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:04.650
to choose depending on how
much flexibility you want

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:08.250
or how specific
your use case is.

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.910
We covered some key factors
that help you decide,

00:06:11.910 --> 00:06:15.480
like whether you do your
inference on the device

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.850
or in the cloud,
and whether you want

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:21.990
to use the pre-trained
models Google provides.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:24.870
Or train and bring
your custom model.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.780
Check out our full session
at Next for a deep dive

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:31.860
analysis, live experiments,
and the latest ML offerings

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:32.790
from Google.

00:06:32.790 --> 00:06:36.740
[MUSIC PLAYING]

